@* What an outreach template's placeholders become, under the box it's written in (Outreach templates). *@
<div class="form-text" id="@Id">
    Placeholders are filled from the action when the email is written, held to the template's TLP ceiling: a part above
    it is left out and named. A placeholder TIDE doesn't know is refused when you save. One with nothing to fill is
    marked for you to deal with before sending, unless you say otherwise (Placeholders, below, shows how).
</div>
<details class="tide-outreach-help small mt-1">
    <summary>Placeholders</summary>
    <div class="tide-field-label mt-2 mb-1">When there's nothing to fill</div>
    <dl class="tide-outreach-placeholders">
        <dt class="tide-data">{{article.other-links?}}</dt>
        <dd>Ending in ?, it's dropped, with its line when nothing else is on it.</dd>
        <dt class="tide-data">{{product.contact|there}}</dt>
        <dd>After a |, the text written instead, as in "Hello {{product.contact|there}},".</dd>
        <dt class="tide-data">{{#article.cves}} … {{else}} … {{/article.cves}}</dt>
        <dd>A section: what's before {{else}} when there's something to fill, what's after it when there isn't. Without
            {{else}}, the whole section goes, so a heading goes with it. A tag alone on its line takes the line with it.
            A section can't hold another.</dd>
    </dl>
    @foreach (var group in OutreachFill.All.GroupBy(p => p.Group))
    {
        <div class="tide-field-label mt-2 mb-1">@group.Key</div>
        <dl class="tide-outreach-placeholders">
            @foreach (var p in group)
            {
                <dt class="tide-data">@p.Written</dt>
                <dd>@p.Description</dd>
            }
        </dl>
    }
</details>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Id { get; set; } = "";
}
